UgxZ0ITOyKP0SNlqXjZ4AaABAg,,False,@GenX-Fossil,"I still remember seeing this for the first time when it dropped. I was thrilled to see Hyunjin's take on ""Beauty and the Beast"" because it's one of my favorite stories. We see the beast when he dances wildly in the castle. Then we get the prince dancing with the rose, the spotlight above looking like the light that shined on the rose under glass. Loved the whole MV then and now.",9,2025-01-01T03:28:16Z,2025-01-01T03:28:16Z
UgxZ0ITOyKP0SNlqXjZ4AaABAg.ACje7Z542M6ACoMmGECIHL,UgxZ0ITOyKP0SNlqXjZ4AaABAg,True,@hitomi2oo710,"Hyunjin never said this was ""beauty & beast"" concept. He actually said it's about his image as a ""prince"" and how he gets more and more disheveled thru the choreography to showcase how he has more depth than just a ""prince"" image. And I saw the vlive when he said that. I also was here when this choreo was released and no one said anything about beauty & beast. Just to make things clear.",1,2025-01-02T23:24:09Z,2025-01-02T23:24:09Z
UgxZ0ITOyKP0SNlqXjZ4AaABAg.ACje7Z542M6ACoXrTeTe15,UgxZ0ITOyKP0SNlqXjZ4AaABAg,True,@GenX-Fossil,"@@hitomi2oo710 But I never said that Hyune named the concept after Beauty & The Beast though. This was MY opinion of the concept; it reminded ME of the fairytale. And when this dropped, I was also there and I did say the same thing back then. Art can be appreciated and perceived differently, even if the creator meant one thing and a viewer sees another. Just to make things clear.",0,2025-01-03T01:00:58Z,2025-01-03T01:00:58Z
