UgwZrv4B7McHJNENJIx4AaABAg,,False,@ssommysom9096,"The fucking story he tells with his choreo. A regal prince, subdued and dignified. But beneath the facade there's a darkness, one woth dark desires. There's a war with himself, afraid of what he'd become if he just gave in. But as the battle wages, he starts to lose ground. The flirty smirk (but still looking princely in the mirror), then the cape comes off, then buttons come undone, and then that deranged smile, signifying that the battle is over, and the noble prince has lost. But the end I think is harder to interpret. To me, the choking motion might be him getting himself a little under control, but still that dangerous expression. To say I'm obsessed is an understatement
(I need a therapist)
The more I watch the more I notice! The way even his walk is like he's fighting himself. The way the moves go from smooth and stately (that ballet-esque move with his hands) to sexy (the rollllll) with jerking pops in between. Then it's like actual fighting, with the kicking and shoving and punching motions! 

The sound of the flames crackling as he sinks to the ground, that's the final blow. When he stands and the music starts to fade in, that's the victor, breathing heavily as it begins to sink in. And then that demented smile of triumph.

The way he starts to move in a more animalistic way, snatching up his trophy with his teeth!!! 
The blue scene represents his desire itself! The misty blue background fading into darkness, giving a sort of dark fantasy vibe! How seductively the figure moves, looking slightly more ""feminine"", but then can claw like an animal. And then it shows the dangerous part (like a succubus, luring you in with beauty only to drain your life), destroying the rose and then that kind of zombie-esque stalk. 

That ""choke"", at the end, like he's composing himself again. But that relaxed little saunter away was not that of the regal prince. 
I dunno man, I just love it. Hyunjin you are truly a genius.",5,2023-11-09T09:03:10Z,2023-11-09T09:53:59Z
