UgxIh8dUFVN72q_ekfF4AaABAg,,False,@benmemon,"(Random story inspired by this)
(Don’t Stan skz so this story doesn’t match up with hyunjins personality)

“Wait no, halt this chaos!” “STOP! YOUVE DESTROYED TOO MUCH” the rightful king heard every plead, he heard every word they muttered once they realized who they really stole the throne from. Well of course “I’m a maniac after listening to the pleads of the people I’ve made vulnerable to just stab them in the back” the king thought to himself. “Who thought it would’ve been a good idea to take away the throne of the righteous?” He chuckled. “It’s your fault, it’s you to blame if you’re shocked that I’m no longer the vulnerable kid who’s throne you thought you could snatch away without worry.”
War the opposing wished for, war they sought for. War they received, war who deceived. War is chaos, so am I. Head in the clouds you all were as you tried biting the ankles of the deities high up above your level. 

The king was madness, even before the climax of the battles he would face. The enemy kingdom’s army cheered at the sight of his kingdom burning to the ground. No, they didn’t win. The fire and destruction wasn’t the accomplishment of the opposing as they thought it would. A feast, they thought to be granted as they went home. There was no victory, it was all the doing of the king. They lost memory of the monarchy who once ruled the kingdom. His family ruled over everything as the royal family. Overthrown his bloodline was, but his power was not to be underestimated.
With every step the army took inside the destroyed palace, the more they were dwelling into his traps. “Steal every once of wealth remaining in this palace!” “Victory to us, we have tamed the foolish competition and gods we shall all be once we arrive home with victory!!”. What victory? What godly status will you receive after foolishly thinking my flames were yours? What kind of prize in heaven awaits when you underestimate the human god himself, me? You are no god. You’re a hill delusionally hoping to be a mountain who pierces the sky with its peak to reach the domain of the gods. You have been doomed since the moment you entered this palace. 
They’ve completed digging their own grave once they’ve entered the kings bedroom. “Oh young prince, how vulnerable you are. You’ll never be able to retake this kingdom”. It’s not like they burned this room down, it was never their achievement. “I made you believe you’ve won when I was just getting started” the king thought while waiting to reveal his precense to the unsuspecting enemies.
They grasped the ornament given to him by his own family, a special mini-crown that meant the world to him as the last embers of his family. Rising from the ashes, the tiny crown flew to the back of the room as the soldiers of the army looked in shock.

“No.. this can’t be.” “You’re dead.. you’re supposed to be!” “Our attacks have lead this kingdom into flames, how were you not killed by such??!?!?” “YOU MONSTER! UNDEAD FIRE-FREAK!” The small and frail prince stood so emotionlessly within the flames as the enemies were throwing insults at him. “What flames? What attacks remained to harm this kingdom aside from my own?” “This is my doing. This destruction is the mere introduction to the horrifying deeds I will do to your kingdom once the time comes” “Oh yeah! I’m not supposed to do this right?” He says as he fends off the spears launched at him with one hand. “Cant you just say sorry to me, of course a child would miss his own family. You think I wouldn’t suspect a thing? This throne will never be yours, since I’m so kind I’ll let you borrow it for the time being” the screams coming from the army would’ve been horrifying to a passerby. He was no passerby, he was the new antagonist of this story. He was never a frail child. He has always been a maniac.

Hol up I’ll finish this later",0,2023-02-08T13:05:29Z,2023-02-09T02:05:33Z
