UgzansmzsxgICBZ7efB4AaABAg,,False,@by_joy,"안녕 baby

How have you been?? 

Are you sleeping?? I'll let it pass if you are too anxious to sleep. Can't wait to see you happy on stage. I know what it means. I'm happier for you than for myself. (I'm pretty excited too)

I've been missing, right? 미안해 

(I swear it wouldn't happen if you had my phone number, I guess kk)

Last week I lost my cellphone in an Uber.

I felt pretty stupid to be honest. It's something I've been feeling lately.

 It happened when I turned 25, it felt like I shouldn't be making some silly mistakes over and over. Like forgetting documents, appointments or paying for stuff. It was something I always heard. Because I don't like to let things, I keep taking responsibilities that in the end I can't handle. I was raised hearing that... so when something like that happened, I looked back at myself and felt like a big child mess.

I have this belief in taking responsibility for my mistakes. That's the most logical thing to do. But... I just lost myself for a moment.

I found the cellphone and solved the situation, but even after I still feel kind of lost. Like I was not moving forward. I reached almost every goal I set when I was 13. 10 years ago... and now, and even more after I met you. I started to see myself different, and freely of the thoughts I was raised by. It doesn't make it easier because I still have to find a way to go. Making silly mistakes made me feel below zero in this process.


I know you had nothing to do with all of this, but every time I come here and look at this keyboard... I feel so vulnerable, I can't hide my feelings. So I was scared.. I guess.. Of coming.

I thought about you every day and every time I cried I imagined your eyes... being honest.. I cried even more when imagining it. It's a safe place that I found and I can't have. 

Still.. receiving any little message, photo, seeing you smile... always warm up my heart and calm down my thoughts. 


My bittersweet
Love you always 

Joy.",1,2022-04-27T23:45:34Z,2022-04-27T23:45:34Z
